 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Musical instruments are grouped by how they make sound:\n• percussion (struck or shaken): the drum, the talking drum, the tam-tam, the balafon, the xylophone, the rattle (maracas), the gong, the bell;\n• string (strings are plucked or bowed): the guitar, the harp, the violin, the mvet (a Beti harp-zither), the kora;\n• wind (you blow into them): the flute, the trumpet, the saxophone, the horn, the whistle;\n• keyboard: the piano, the keyboard (electronic), the organ.\nPeople: a drummer, a guitarist, a pianist, a flautist, a band, an orchestra.\nDrawing task: in your exercise book, draw two instruments from your region and label their parts (for example: drum — body, skin, ropes; guitar — body, neck, strings, sound hole).",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {},
  "problem": "To which group does the mvet belong?",
  "steps": [
   "The mvet has strings that are plucked.",
   "Instruments with strings belong to the string group."
  ],
  "answer": "the string instruments",
  "checks": []
 },
